From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH] desktop/index.html: keep CJK button labels inside their buttons

The shared Button component renders <button class="inline-flex ...">
at fixed heights (h-6 = 24px and friends) and never disables wrapping.
When a flex row runs out of room — the Settings > Diagnostics form is
the repro — a CJK label with no other break opportunity (the zh-CN
"Refresh" / "Rebuild local index" buttons) folds onto two lines; the
two line boxes (~27px) overrun the button's fixed height and the
glyphs paint outside its border (Range.getClientRects() showed 2 line
boxes against a 24px button box).

button.inline-flex{white-space:nowrap} keeps every label on one line,
and via min-content sizing flex can no longer shrink a button below
its label width — the row gives ground elsewhere instead of clipping
glyphs. The rule is global to the shared Button component; a post-fix
scan over every button in the app found zero wrapped labels, and
Latin labels never wrapped to begin with (they break at spaces).

Same tag id and rules as the in-place hotfix baked into the shipped
Offline installer's dist/index.html (<style id="cjk-btn-nowrap">).

diff --git a/desktop/index.html b/desktop/index.html
index 21e889c..c56c4a0 100644
--- a/desktop/index.html
+++ b/desktop/index.html
@@ -721,6 +721,7 @@
       })()
     </script>
     <style id="h5-host-input-fix">div:has(> div > div > #h5-access-public-url){container-type:inline-size}@container (max-width: 28rem){div:has(> div > #h5-access-public-url){grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)!important}}</style>
+    <style id="cjk-btn-nowrap">button.inline-flex{white-space:nowrap}</style>
   </head>
   <body>
     <div id="root"></div>
